[agent] - **Transformation:** for each feature, `(x - mean) / std`, using the **training-rows-only** mean and **population** standard deviation (`STDDEV_POP`, no Bessel correction), applied to both splits; values `ROUND`ed to 6 decimals. Verified correct: the train-split means of all four standardized features round to `0.0`.
[agent] This is the offline (BigQuery) backing that Vertex AI Feature Store would reference.
[agent] **What the interface CANNOT do — missing capability:**
[agent] The remaining required steps — *registering* this BigQuery table as a Vertex AI **Feature Group** (the "feature table, version 1, record key `row_id`") and making its features available for **low-latency/online lookup** (a **FeatureOnlineStore** + **FeatureView**, the online-vs-offline distinction the task asks for) — are **not reachable through the allowed interface**.
[agent] - The GA `gcloud ai` surface exposes only: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. There is **no** `feature-groups`, `feature-online-stores`, `feature-views`, or `featurestores` group (all return `Invalid choice`).
[agent] - The Vertex AI Feature Registry / Feature Store commands live only under **`gcloud beta ai …`** / **`gcloud alpha ai …`**, and those channels are **hard-blocked** by the environment (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`).
[agent] Because the feature-store registration and online-serving commands are absent from GA `gcloud ai` and beta/alpha are blocked, I cannot register the Vertex feature table or create the online store/feature view through the interface. Per the task's guidance, I did not build a local or off-interface workaround.
